# Session transcripts — local working artifacts, not source
omo-psmux-bridge.md

# Agent tooling state. `.omo/` is scratch: session transcripts, run-continuation
# pointers, drafts. None of it is a record this repository keeps.
#
# `.omo/evidence/` is the deliberate exception and IS tracked, wholesale. This is
# not a tidy-up allowance for one or two cited files — it is the evidence
# directory. 16 of the 19 `task-*` files here are cited by CONTRACT.md or by
# `scripts/windows/bin/omo-opencode-port.ps1`, which SHIPS in the release
# archive, so a shipped script points at evidence that has to exist. CONTRACT.md
# also rejects any measurement whose run left nothing under version control.
#
# They were previously force-added with `git add -f`, leaving them
# tracked-but-claimed-ignored: the rule and the index disagreed, so the next
# `git clean -xfd` or a fresh clone disagreed too. Naming the exception makes
# the two agree on purpose. Tracking the directory rather than a hand-picked
# subset also avoids the opposite trap, where uncited siblings sit untracked and
# visible, one `git add -A` away from being committed by accident.
.omo/*
!.omo/evidence/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Build output
dist/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Pinned upstream source checkouts used to verify CONTRACT.md citations.
# `.contract/psmux` is a full git clone (21M, own .git) pinned to the commit
# recorded in scripts/contract/pins.json. `bun run contract:fetch` recreates it.
# It must never be committed: it is a vendored upstream tree, not this project's
# source, and its .git would turn it into a broken nested repo.
.contract/